The scatter plot shows advertising spend (hundreds of dollars) and monthly sales (thousands of dollars) for $9$ stores, with a line of best fit.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, xscale=0.75, yscale=0.23]
\draw[->] (0,0)--(10.5,0);
\draw[->] (0,0)--(0,37);
\foreach \x in {0,2,4,6,8,10} {\node[below,font=\scriptsize] at (\x,0) {$\x$};}
\foreach \y in {5,10,15,20,25,30} {\node[left,font=\scriptsize] at (-0.3,\y) {$\y$};}
\node[left,font=\scriptsize] at (-0.3,0) {$0$};
\foreach \p in {(1,7),(2,10),(3,13),(4,15),(5,18),(6,21),(7,23),(8,26)} {\fill \p circle (2.2pt);}
\fill (1.5,23) circle (2.2pt);
\draw[thick,blue] (0.5,11.75)--(9,24.5);
\node[rotate=90,font=\scriptsize] at (-1.7,18) {Sales (thousands)};
\node[below,font=\scriptsize] at (5,-4.5) {Spend (hundreds)};
\node[font=\small] at (5,35) {Spend vs sales};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Which point is the outlier?

